# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify header rules

# ── Security ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A static site has no database, no login, no server-side code, so the
# attacks that matter are content injection, clickjacking, and downgrade
# to plain HTTP. These close those off.
#
# script-src is now a bare 'self' — there are no inline scripts left in
# any page, so no hash or nonce is needed and injected script simply
# cannot run. If you ever add an inline <script>, it will be blocked
# until you add its sha256 hash here. That is the intended behaviour.
# (JSON-LD blocks are type="application/ld+json", never executed, and
# are unaffected.)

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; script-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://formspree.io; form-action https://formspree.io; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), midi=(), magnetometer=(), accelerometer=(), gyroscope=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400

# HSTS is deliberately one day, not one year. It tells browsers to refuse
# plain HTTP for this domain, and they cache that instruction — so if a
# certificate ever broke, the site would be unreachable for the full
# duration with no way to click past. One day means a bad day, not a bad
# year. Once it has run happily for a few weeks, raise it to 31536000.
# Only add `preload` if you're certain; that one is effectively permanent.


# ── Caching ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Short while the site is still changing, so an edit shows up on the next
# reload rather than days later. Costs a little speed, saves confusion.
#
# Note Cloudflare applies EVERY matching rule and concatenates them rather
# than picking the most specific — overlapping globs produce two conflicting
# Cache-Control values. Keep these patterns non-overlapping.

/photos/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate

/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate


# ── At launch ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Once the photographs and copy settle, swap the three blocks above for
# these. Repeat visits get much faster.
#
# /photos/*
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
#
# /css/*
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
#
# /js/*
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
